From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:45:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: preserve native radio translations
 across system sleep

The J713 radio DART loses its register state while its live page tables
remain in memory. Let the PCIe host own its stop and restore
transaction, with mapping writers fenced while bus mastering and the
port are held. Restore translation, fault-mask and stream state before
admitting DMA.

Restrict the provider to the managed J713 radio DART. Reject corrupt
snapshots and retain the closed DMA boundary after an incomplete
restore. Add fault-injection coverage for writer exclusion, snapshots
and power loss.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[niteria: the DART fw and range host tests' mocks now have the sleep record and writer gate]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 86eb9a2d06703f2d839d4d65ae8d25ebf1d440f0)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
